      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Standard bench and clinical research approaches alone are not well suited to account for this complexity, as most cancer control interventions often focus on explicit, often linear health outcomes of a specific, well-defined population [1, 8, 9]. The extent to which system dynamics modeling has been applied specifically to cancer prevention and control has not been studied.",
      "reason": "Describes current knowledge limitations and identifies a specific gap in research."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "To overcome persistent barriers to providing high-quality, equitable care, approaches are needed to address this complexity and provide guidance for successful intervention. System dynamics is a multifaceted systems science approach for analyzing the complex interrelationships between variables in a system and the resulting nonlinear system behavior.",
      "reason": "Explains the need for new approaches and introduces system dynamics as a solution, justifying the review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No similar systematic reviews for cancer prevention and control are indicated; the evidence mentions past reviews in related fields but not specifically for cancer, and the review addresses a gap without citing previous similar reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review is a methods review and does not assess intervention effects, as stated in the methods section (chunk text_5)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
